.Dd October 21, 2026
.Dt HALFCONSOLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halfconsole
.Nd HalfBSD local console account selection
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is launched only by PID 1 as root on console sessions whose tty entry uses
.Pa /etc/rc.console .
Lua mode substitutes this helper without executing that RC script.
It preserves the controlling terminal and replaces itself with native
.Xr login 1 ,
retaining PAM session setup, groups, home directory and logout behavior.
It does not supervise login or create a desktop session.
.Pp
The trusted
.Pa /etc/halfbsd/system.lua
may contain
.Bd -literal -offset indent
console={user='charlie',autologin=true,select_timeout=3}
.Ed
.Pp
Defaults are root, automatic login and a three-second selection deadline.
Enter another existing login account followed by Return to select it, or
enter login to request authenticated login. Empty input selects the default.
A zero timeout selects the default immediately.
Set autologin=false for authenticated login without selection.
These settings grant passwordless access to the designated physical console;
SSH authentication and other getty terminals remain unchanged.
.Pp
When console policy is absent, literal console_user assignments in trusted
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
and
.Pa /etc/rc.conf.local
are recognized, in that order, with a migration warning.
Shell expressions and indirect configuration are not evaluated.
Move the intended account into the Lua console table to complete migration.
Administrator files are never rewritten.
.Pp
Invalid accounts, unsupported legacy expressions and selection failures use
authenticated login rather than silently selecting root.
Configuration rejected earlier by the boot manager can instead enter native
recovery before console sessions start.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr halfinit 8 ,
.Xr init 8
